  {
    "id": "static-moire",
    "title": "Static Moiré",
    "description": [
"The <i>Static Moiré</i> series explores visual interference created entirely through the viewer's presence. Built from distinctly separate, layered surfaces held at a spatial distance, the works generate dynamic moiré patterns as a spectator moves through space. Operating without motors or electronics, the object's physical stillness turns human movement into the catalyst for change.",

"By decoupling motion from the artwork itself, the experience shifts entirely to how the layers align from different angles and distances. Viewers are invited to explore the piece dynamically, where every step, shift in perspective, or change in proximity uncovers new optical configurations within the stationary layers."
],
