  {
    "id": "kinetic-moire",
    "title": "Kinetic Moiré",
    "description": [
"The <i>Kinetic Moiré</i> series is the result from five years of experimentation with physical motion and optical interference. Composed of layered, rotating discs painted with spiraling patterns, the works generate continuously shifting waves and forms. As the physical layers spin against one another, moiré patterns emerge, evolve, and dissolve across the moving surfaces.",
"Parametric design is used to previsualize potential interference outcomes and generate files for digital fabrication. Translating the digital work into physical materials allows the optical experience to react directly to human presence, making the final visual outcome entirely dependent on the perspective of the viewer."],
