  {
    "id": "interference",
    "title": "Interference",
    "description": [
"In the Interference series, printmaking serves as a method for exploring variation within structured systems. Algorithmic processes and parametric design help navigate the initial uncertainty of creation, beginning with a simple spiral and incrementally introducing complexity. This approach mirrors the physical refinement of a ceramicist at the wheel, where subtle adjustments dramatically alter the final form. Through code, endless variations are generated, which are then curated and translated into physical prints.",
"Rather than pursuing a single resolved image, the work emphasizes iteration and selection. By layering multiple impressions of a single matrix with linear and rotational offsets, printmaking becomes a tactile space for discovering interference and resonance. The resulting prints bridge computational precision and the unpredictable nuances of physical process, a dynamic where structure and chance remain in constant negotiation." ],
